      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "73cb6792-2ddb-54dc-ad69-a95608d375f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Balan, T.I., Rihanna, Radu Sîrbu, Arsenie Todiraș, Gary Brolsma\n- Music Groups and Songs: O-Zone, \"Live Your Life,\" \"Paper Trail,\" \"Dragostea Din Tei\"\n- Topics: Grammy nominations, Internet memes\n\nFacts:\n- O-Zone was a Moldovan pop music trio active from 1998 to 2005.\n- O-Zone consisted of Dan Balan, Radu Sîrbu, and Arsenie Todiraș.\n- \"Live Your Life\" is a song by American rapper T.I. from his 2008 sixth studio album \"Paper Trail\" and features Barbadian singer Rihanna.\n- Dan Balan was nominated for a Grammy as a co-writer of Rihanna and T.I.'s \"Live Your Life,\" making him the first and only Moldovan musician to receive such a nomination.\n- The Internet meme \"Numa Numa\" is based on a video by American vlogger Gary Brolsma made after O-Zone's performance of the song \"Dragostea Din Tei.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
